  "body": "Follow-up from the high-tier review of PR #1191 (merged; its last review comment, 2026-11-12). Not a defect in the rule - a gap in its pin.\n\n`lathe_workholding_mill_post::every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict` walks 24 cells (machine none/mill, mill-turn, lathe x post voice turning, milling, undeclared x section work-spindle, milling, C) but asserts only 15. The other 9 are combinations whose operation cannot be created on that machine; the test skips them without asserting that creation is what refuses them. So the arm \"milling post + lathe-refused section on a plain lathe -> judged\" in `work_speed` (`crates/app/src/commands/setup_workholding.rs`) has no pin, and a later change that made one of the 9 creatable would go unjudged without a red test.\n\nAlso from that review, for whoever takes this: an on-centre drill on a mill-turn through a milling post is now refused over the limit even on a control whose M3 drives the tool spindle - the safe side; leave it unless a user hits it (it belongs with #1199's question).\n\nDone means: each of the 9 skipped cells asserts WHY it is skipped (the creation refusal, by its message), and the plain-lathe milling-post arm has a pin that reaches `work_speed`; no rule changes.\n",
